ion of AKT1 o...", "text": "Suppression of PKN2 eliminates the phosphorylation of AKT1 on serine-308, indicating that PKN2 is probably the responsible kinase (Jin et al. 2021). Activity of PI3K, which produces phosphatidylinositol-3,4,5-trisphosphate, is not required for AKT1 phosphorylation on serine-308 (Jin et al. 2021). Phosphorylation of AKT1 on serine-473 by mTORC2 increases phosphorylation of serine-308 by PDPK1 (PDK1) (Sarbassov et al. 2005). AKT1 phosphorylated on serine-308 and serine-473 is located at the plasma membrane at cell-cell junctions in endothelial cells experiencing unidirectional laminar shear stress, but it is perinuclear in cells experiencing disturbed flow (Melchior and Frangos 2014).", "literatureReference": [199373], "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "isChimeric": false, "category": "transition", "catalystActivity": [{"dbId": 9860822, "displayName": "protein tyrosine kinase activity of p-T816-PKN2 [cytosol]", "catalyzedEvent": [9860759], "physicalEntity": {"dbId": 5623652, "displayName": "p-T816-PKN2 [cytosol]", "stId": "R-HSA-5623652", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-5623652.1", "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["p-T816-PKN2", "p-T816-PRK2"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "catalystActivities": [9860822], "endCoordinate": 984, "referenceType": "ReferenceGeneProduct", "startCoordinate": 1, "className": "Protein", "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "EntityWithAccessionedSequence"}, "className": "CatalystActivity", "schemaClass": "CatalystActivity"}], "input": [{"dbId": 377272, "displayName": "p-S473-AKT1:PIP3 [plasma membrane]", "stId": "R-HSA-377272", "stIdVersion": "R-HSA-377272.1", "maxDepth": 2, "name": ["p-S473-AKT1:PIP3"], "speciesName": "Homo sapiens", "consumedByEvent": [9860759], "species": [48887], "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "Complex", "c